<title>UK: Hanson rules out early Eastern sale - report.</title>
<headline>Hanson rules out early Eastern sale - report.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-12-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>Hanson Plc has ruled out a trade sale of Eastern Group, the UK arm of its soon-to-be-floated Energy Group, the Financial Times said on Thursday.</p>
<p>It quoted Energy Group chairman Derek Bonham as saying there was not &quot;a snowball's chance in hell&quot; of Eastern being sold separately before the February demerger.</p>
<p>The report said some analysts had argued that Eastern has little in common with Peabody, Hanson's U.S. coal unit with which it is being bracketed for the flotation.</p>
<p>--London Newsroom +44 171 542 7717</p>
